  "body": "Previously, the specification included a list of 106 named character references which don't end with a semicolon. Now, this list is missing.\n\nSome text in the specification still implies that some named character references may not end with a semicolon:\n\n<blockquote>Otherwise, a character reference is parsed. If the last character matched is not a U+003B SEMICOLON character (;), there is a parse error.</blockquote>\n\n\n> If the markup contains (not in an attribute) the string `I'm &notit; I tell you`, the character reference is parsed as \"not\", as in, `I'm ¬it; I tell you` (and this is a parse error).\n",
